# Phase 10 Walkthrough — Observability, Metrics, Health Monitoring & Load Testing

## Overview of What Was Built
1. **Prometheus Metrics Registry & Custom Telemetry ([server/src/utils/metrics.ts](file:///c:/Users/arpit/OneDrive/Documents/HTML/React/OnlineCodeHelp/server/src/utils/metrics.ts))**:
   - Integrated `prom-client` with standard Node.js runtime collection (event loop delay, heap/RSS memory, GC cycles, active handles).
   - **HTTP Telemetry**: `codejudge_http_requests_total` counter and `codejudge_http_request_duration_seconds` histogram parameterized with route, method, and status. Implemented dynamic route normalizer (`/api/problems/:id` masking) to protect against cardinality explosion.
   - **Queue Depth Gauges**: `codejudge_queue_jobs_gauge` tracking BullMQ `waiting`, `active`, `completed`, `failed`, and `delayed` job counts.
   - **Execution Engine Telemetry**: `codejudge_submissions_total` tracking accepted/rejected incoming jobs, `codejudge_submission_verdicts_total` tracking verdicts (`ACCEPTED`, `WRONG_ANSWER`, `TIME_LIMIT_EXCEEDED`, `COMPILATION_ERROR`), and `codejudge_submission_duration_seconds` histogram for execution times.
   - **Cache & Security Telemetry**: `codejudge_cache_operations_total` (hit/miss/set/del tracking) and `codejudge_rate_limit_rejections_total`.
   - Exposed Prometheus standard scrape target at `GET /api/metrics`.

2. **Deep Health & Readiness Probes ([server/src/index.ts](file:///c:/Users/arpit/OneDrive/Documents/HTML/React/OnlineCodeHelp/server/src/index.ts))**:
   - **Liveness Probe (`GET /api/health`)**: Lightweight check exposing uptime, timestamps, and process memory utilization (`heapUsedMb`, `heapTotalMb`, `rssMb`).
   - **Readiness Probe (`GET /api/ready`)**: Deep dependency inspection actively executing:
     - PostgreSQL ping: `SELECT 1` query.
     - Redis ping: Client `ping()` command.
     - BullMQ queue readiness: Client connection status validation.
     - Returns HTTP 200 OK when 100% operational, or HTTP 503 Service Unavailable with degraded subsystem status breakdown if any dependency is down.
   - **Diagnostic Endpoint (`GET /api/system/status`)**: Exposes live BullMQ counts, process memory, and dependency statuses.

3. **Frontend Real-Time Telemetry Modal ([client/src/components/SystemHealthModal.tsx](file:///c:/Users/arpit/OneDrive/Documents/HTML/React/OnlineCodeHelp/client/src/components/SystemHealthModal.tsx))**:
   - Bespoke glassmorphic modal embedded in navigation bar with an animated pulsing indicator.
   - Polls `/api/ready` and `/api/system/status` every 3 seconds.
   - Visual gauges and badges for PostgreSQL, Redis, and BullMQ cluster health.
   - Live queue metrics breakdown (waiting, active docker sandboxes, completed, failed).
   - Real-time Node.js heap memory tracking.

4. **Concurrency & Stress Load Testing Suite ([server/scripts/load_test.ps1](file:///c:/Users/arpit/OneDrive/Documents/HTML/React/OnlineCodeHelp/server/scripts/load_test.ps1))**:
   - Automated multi-request concurrent burst generator against `/api/submissions`.
   - Measures end-to-end burst duration, throughput (req/sec), latency percentiles (average and p95), rate-limit backpressure response, and queue drain duration.

